// Failure golden: a constructor payload violating its declared field type
// (ADR-80 Decision 4/5; ADR-54 §3).
// (Pathological tree: testing artifact, not pedagogy -- ADR-52 Decision C.)
//
// `Some(x: a)` of `Maybe(a)`, ascribed `Maybe(Integer)`, instantiates the field
// `a` to `Integer`; a `String` payload therefore fails to check. The frozen
// core carries only the constructor's nominal tag (not its field types), so the
// 1-cell MVP enforces field discipline at the pipeline seam: the payload is
// checked against its declared field type instantiated at the ascribed
// arguments, exactly the soundness a tag-only rule cannot express. Without it
// `Some("hello") : Maybe(Integer)` would wrongly type-check.
data Maybe(a : Type) : Type {
  None : Maybe(a);
  Some : (x : a) --> Maybe(a);
}

(Some("hello") : Maybe(Integer))

//@ expect-diagnostic: type mismatch
